i(17,"p"),r(18,"The "),i(19,"strong"),r(20,"Incubator"),n(),r(21," at "),i(22,"strong"),r(23,"Amity University Noida,"),n(),r(24," represents a strong commitment to nurturing innovation, entrepreneurship, and scalable enterprise creation. With a presence in "),i(25,"strong"),r(26,"17 cities across India and 5 countries worldwide"),n(),r(27,", the Incubator has evolved into a truly global ecosystem that supports start-ups, innovators, and early-stage ventures at every step of their entrepreneurial journey."),n(),i(28,"p"),r(29,"Designed as a launchpad for ideas with impact, the Incubator brings together academic insight, industry expertise, mentorship, and infrastructure to help innovators convert concepts into viable, market-ready solutions. Its widespread geographic footprint enables entrepreneurs to access local market insights while remaining connected to a global network of knowledge, investment, and opportunity."),n(),i(30,"h5"),r(31,"A Pan-India and Global Entrepreneurial Network"),n(),i(32,"p"),r(33,"The Incubator\u2019s presence across 17 Indian cities ensures that innovation is not limited to a single campus or region. Entrepreneurs from diverse geographies, backgrounds, and sectors are able to benefit from structured incubation support, regardless of where they are located. This decentralised model encourages regional innovation, supports local problem-solving, and enables start-ups to address context-specific challenges with scalable solutions."),n(),i(34,"p"),r(35,"Beyond India, the Incubator\u2019s footprint across 5 countries positions it as a globally connected innovation platform. This international presence allows start-ups to explore cross-border markets, understand global business environments, and engage with international mentors, investors, and partners. Such exposure is critical for ventures aiming to build globally relevant products and services."),n(),i(36,"h5"),r(37,"Supporting Start-ups Across the Lifecycle"),n(),i(38,"p"),r(39,"The Incubator is structured to support entrepreneurs at multiple stages\u2014from ideation and early validation to growth and scale-up. Innovators receive guidance on refining business models, conducting market research, developing prototypes, and creating sustainable go-to-market strategies. This structured support reduces early-stage risk and increases the likelihood of long-term success. "),n(),i(40,"p"),r(41,"Through access to expert mentorship, legal and intellectual property guidance, and business advisory services, the Incubator ensures that start-ups are well-prepared to navigate the complexities of entrepreneurship. Regular interactions with industry leaders and domain experts help founders gain practical insights and avoid common pitfalls."),n(),i(42,"h5"),r(43,"Infrastructure, Mentorship, and Ecosystem Support"),n(),i(44,"p"),r(45,"A key strength of the Incubator lies in its integrated ecosystem. Entrepreneurs gain access to co-working spaces, innovation labs, testing facilities, and technology support that enable rapid experimentation and product development. These resources are complemented by a strong mentorship network comprising experienced entrepreneurs, academicians, investors, and corporate leaders."),n(),i(46,"p"),r(47,"Mentorship is tailored to the specific needs of each start-up, ensuring personalised guidance and measurable progress. This hands-on approach helps founders sharpen their vision, strengthen execution capabilities, and build resilient enterprises."),n(),i(48,"h5"),r(49,"Enabling Innovation with Social and Economic Impact"),n(),i(50,"p"),r(51,"The Incubator actively encourages innovations that address real-world challenges and contribute to sustainable development. Many supported ventures focus on areas such as technology-enabled services, healthcare, education, sustainability, agriculture, fintech, and digital transformation. By aligning innovation with societal needs, the Incubator ensures that entrepreneurship leads to meaningful and inclusive growth."),n(),i(52,"p"),r(53,"Its global reach further amplifies impact, allowing start-ups to adapt solutions across markets and cultures. This exposure strengthens the ability of ventures to scale responsibly while remaining sensitive to local needs."),n(),i(54,"h5"),r(55,"A Platform for Collaboration and Growth"),n(),i(56,"p"),r(57,"With its extensive presence across cities and countries, the Incubator serves as a hub for collaboration. Start-ups benefit from peer learning, networking opportunities, demo days, and investor interactions that open doors to funding and partnerships. Connections with academic institutions, research centres, and industry bodies further enrich the entrepreneurial experience. "),n(),i(58,"p"),r(59,"The Incubator also acts as a bridge between academia and enterprise, translating research and innovation into commercially viable ventures. This synergy between knowledge creation and entrepreneurship strengthens the overall innovation ecosystem."),n(),i(60,"h5"),r(61,"Shaping the Future of Entrepreneurship"),n(),i(62,"p"),r(63,"By combining global reach with local relevance, the Incubator plays a pivotal role in shaping future-ready entrepreneurs. Its presence in 17 cities across India and 5 countries worldwide reflects a vision of inclusive, scalable, and globally connected innovation."),n(),i(64,"p"),r(65,"Through structured support, mentorship, and access to a powerful ecosystem, the Incubator continues to empower innovators to transform ideas into impactful enterprises\u2014driving economic growth, job creation, and technological progress at both national and global levels."),n()(),i(66,"div",10)(67,"div",11),m(68,"img",12),i(69,"p")(70,"b"),r(71,"A vibrant, informal collaboration space designed to spark creativity and open dialogue. "),n()()()(),i(72,"div",10)(73,"div",11),m(74,"img",13),i(75,"p")(76,"b"),r(77,"A thoughtfully designed co-working area that supports teamwork, ideation, and early-stage startup discussions."),n()()()()